<https://aciege.org/concept/term/426_66> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "INDUSTRIE CULTURELLE SECTEUR"@fr ;
    skos:notation "426_66" ;
    skos:definition "Déf 1« L'industrie culturelle comprend les domaines liés au tourisme, au design, aux nouveaux médias ainsi qu'à l'informatique et à la communication, au spectacle et à la culture. » Source : © Finnfacts 2001. http://www.finnfacts.com/ (consulté le 1er juin 2005) Déf 2« The cultural industry committee has defined the concept of cultural industry on several levels. According to the most general definition, cultural industry is production based on meaning contents. This general definition covers traditional commodity production marketed by cultural meaning, e.g. clothing or any kind of brand product.» Source : Ministry of Education Finland. Cultural Industry Committee. Final Report (2004). http://www.minedu.fi (consulté le 1er juin 2005)"@fr ;
    dct:source "© Finnfacts 2001. http://www.finnfacts.com/ (consulté le 1er juin 2005) Déf 2« The cultural industry committee has defined the concept of cultural industry on several levels. According to the most general definition, cultural industry is production based on meaning contents. This general definition covers traditional commodity production marketed by cultural meaning, e.g. clothing or any kind of brand product. | Ministry of Education Finland. Cultural Industry Committee. Final Report (2004). http://www.minedu.fi (consulté le 1er juin 2005)." ;
